---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Reader — questions" description="Reader saves links for use with ChatGPT." canonicalPath="/faq">
  <div class="page"><header class="header"><div class="header-inner"><a class="brand" href="/">Reader</a><a class="btn-signin" href="/library">Inbox</a></div></header>
  <main class="hero" style="display:block;max-width:48rem"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h1>Just your saved links.</h1>
    <h2>How do I add one?</h2><p>Paste a URL in the inbox or click Save link in the Chrome extension.</p>
    <h2>How does ChatGPT use it?</h2><p>Connect Reader through MCP with OAuth. ChatGPT can search links, retrieve available text, and mark links read when you ask. The connection requires a deployed endpoint and OAuth setup.</p>
    <h2>Where are the other features?</h2><p>RSS, the reader view, annotations, boards, memories, PDFs, and built-in AI are outside the active product. Existing saved data is retained.</p>
    <h2>Where is the extension?</h2><p>It is built from this repository and loaded unpacked in Chrome. Public distribution is deferred.</p>
  </main><footer class="site-footer"><a href="/">Reader</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></footer></div>
</Layout>
